text":"It then hit 14th-placed Jacques Laffite's Ligier, sending both Pryce and Laffite head-on into the catch fencing and a concrete wall.","q":true,"src":"Wikipedia","c":19},{"lap":78,"text":"The order at the front stayed put until lap seven when Lauda took the lead and was never passed again, with Scheckter taking second from Hunt 11 laps later.","q":true,"src":"Wikipedia","c":0},{"lap":78,"text":"Despite this, Lauda held on to win his first victory since his near-fatal crash at the 1976 German Grand Prix the previous year.","q":true,"src":"Wikipedia","c":0},{"lap":78,"text":"South African Scheckter was second, and Patrick Depailler's six-wheeler took third from Hunt in the closing laps.","q":true,"src":"Wikipedia","c":2}],"x":{"drivers":[],"cars":[{"id":"brm_1977","ref":"brm","name":"BRM","year":1977,"pace":2.544,"pace_sd":0.5,"deg_rel":0.0,"n_races":9,"p_mech_lap":0.007,"colours":null,"source":"history"}]}}